Sent SMS stayed "pending" in the event log for ever.

Conversations logs a message it sent with RTCOM_EL_FLAG_SMS_PENDING and
keeps its token as the event's "message-token" header; the delivery
report (telepathy-ring's, once the modem has sent the SMS) names that
token as its original, and Conversations then clears the flag. The token
was taken from the sent message's header (Tp::Message::messageToken()),
but telepathy-glib's message mixin passes it only as MessageSent's
argument, not in the header: the header stayed empty, nothing was stored,
and every report ended in "the original message for this delivery report
was not found". Now the sent token (Tp-Qt's sentMessageToken) is taken
when the header has none.

Found in the FreeBSD port (freebsd/hildon/patches/conversations/0001,
freebsd/modem/README.md); Leste's Conversations 0.7.87 has the same code.

diff --git a/src/lib/tp/tp.cpp b/src/lib/tp/tp.cpp
index 01f02fb..218c1ec 100644
--- a/src/lib/tp/tp.cpp
+++ b/src/lib/tp/tp.cpp
@@ -741,7 +741,14 @@ void TelepathyAccount::onMessageSent(const Tp::Message &message, Tp::MessageSend
   if (result.isNull()) {
     qWarning() << "Failed to add a database event";
   } else {
-    if (auto message_token = message.messageToken().toStdString(); !message_token.empty())
+    // the token the connection manager gave the message (MessageSent's
+    // token): telepathy-glib's message mixin does not put it in the sent
+    // message's header, so messageToken() is empty for ring's SMS, and the
+    // delivery report (whose original token it is) found no message
+    auto message_token = message.messageToken().toStdString();
+    if (message_token.empty())
+      message_token = sentMessageToken.toStdString();
+    if (!message_token.empty())
       rtcom_qt::set_event_header(result->event_id(), "message-token", message_token);
   }
 }
